    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d204">

                <pb facs="0293" n="173" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg173"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Rockhill to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1905-12-05"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 5, 1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 163.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 130 of October
                    26, 1905, informing you that I had effected an agreement with the Dutch minister
                    for the reciprocal protection of trade-marks in China, I now have the honor to
                    inform you that on November 27 last a similar agreement was made with the chargé
                    d’affaires of Belgium.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to inclose herewith copies of the notes exchanged with the
                    Belgian representative.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d204-a1.xml" xpointer="d204-a1"/>
